rid-gutless-myna introduced the inaccurate successful-cycle wording and requires an append-only correction.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Make the implementation skill use atomic `rebar claim` with the conditional identity guidance established by F15.\n- Remove direct `transition open in_progress` as a claim alternative.\n- State in the brainstorm skill that blocked work defers plan review until it becomes claimable.\n- State that unsigned `INDETERMINATE` is not a successful review verdict.\n- Preserve dependency order and the prohibition on agent force.\n- Append a historical correction to arid-gutless-myna without rewriting its existing record.\n- Run focused skill frontmatter, synchronization, and workflow guidance checks.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The implementation skill requires atomic claim for starting work.\n- [ ] The implementation skill uses the F15 identity fallback and does not prescribe a bare handle.\n- [ ] The brainstorm skill defers review for blocked work until the ticket becomes claimable.\n- [ ] The brainstorm skill states that unsigned `INDETERMINATE` is not a successful verdict.\n- [ ] Both skills retain dependency-order and no-agent-force guidance.\n- [ ] arid-gutless-myna contains an append-only correction that cites the enforced behavior.\n- [ ] Focused skill contract checks pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md","reason":"Correct atomic claim and identity guidance."},{"path":"examples/agent-skills/rebar-brainstorm/SKILL.md","reason":"Correct blocked plan review and unsigned verdict guidance."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_agent_skill_ticket_workflow_guidance.py","reason":"Pin the corrected workflow contracts in focused tests."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","20f3-56b5-6e97-4de3"],["parent","b8bf-a5aa-2f4d-44d4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"b8bf-a5aa-2f4d-44d4","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"plan